<<~ ahu #/entry>>

! Each Evidence Source Testifies Within Its Frame

The Loom carries source bytes by SHA-256, records native coordinates, and keeps
`source` / `inferred` / `proposed` as distinct epistemic states. A raster with
nodata cannot testify about its blank cells. A local model-unit coordinate
cannot testify about meters. Two pixels, no matter their resemblance, do not
alone measure the hidden side of a fortress.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/rules>>

!! Registration and Measurement

* ''Native data first.'' Read raster transforms, masks, and coordinate frames from actual bytes before comparing their claims.
* ''Survey anchors testify.'' A control fit enters verified state only after a digest-checked source supplies training and independent held-out pairs, with residuals below an explicit tolerance. Even that result certifies only its declared transformation, not another camera.
* ''Guard height datum.'' A horizontal CRS transform cannot quietly convert vertical datums. Unknown datum carries unknown authority.
* ''Null gives information.'' Empty masks, symmetric calibration objects, unobserved features, and missing witnesses mark ambiguity, not success.
* ''Keep errors distinct.'' A wrong fit, corrupted source, and failed CAD body require different rejection receipts.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/links>>

Current executable boundaries and tests live in `projection_loom/evidence_receipts.py` and the test suite. Historical measurement-contract and research-register testimony is recoverable through the pinned Git archive.

<<~/ahu>>

